-- title:
--   One non-central approximable element suffices at a split place
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb Q$ be nonzero, write $B=\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$, and let $O\subseteq B$ be a $\mathbb Z$-submodule that is an order in the sense of [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsOrder`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_Order.html#L11): $1\in O$, $O$ is closed under multiplication, its $\mathbb Q$-span is all of $B$, and it is finitely generated. Let $w$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$, with completion $\mathbb Q_w$. Assume $B\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_w$ contains an element that is nonzero and not a unit. Call an element $t\in B\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_w$ *of reduced norm one* if for every ring isomorphism $\varphi\colon B\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_w\to\mathbb H[\mathbb Q_w,a,b]$ satisfying $\varphi(z\otimes r)=r\cdot(z\ \text{coordinatewise in}\ \mathbb Q_w)$ one has $\mathrm{nrd}(\varphi t)=1$, where $\mathrm{nrd}(x)=x_0^2-ax_1^2-bx_2^2+abx_3^2$; and call $t$ *approximable* if for every $M\in\mathbb N$, $M\neq 0$, there is $\beta\in B$ with $\mathrm{nrd}\,\beta=1$ such that $\beta\otimes 1=1+M\cdot z$ with $z\in\mathrm{localBox}\,O\,w'$ for every height-one prime $w'\neq w$, and $\beta\otimes 1=t+M\cdot z$ with $z\in\mathrm{localBox}\,O\,w$ at $w$ itself, where $\mathrm{localBox}\,O\,v$ is the additive subgroup of $B\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v$ generated by the elements $z\otimes c$ with $z\in O$ and $c$ in the valuation ring of $\mathbb Q_v$. The assertion is: if some approximable element of reduced norm one is distinct from $1$ and from $-1$, then every element $s'$ of reduced norm one is approximable.
--
--   This is the normal-subgroup step in Kneser's approach to strong approximation for the reduced-norm-one group of a quaternion algebra over $\mathbb Q$ at a finite place $w$ where the algebra splits: the approximable norm-one elements form a conjugation-stable subgroup of $(B\otimes\mathbb Q_w)^1\cong\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Q_w)$, so it is everything as soon as it contains a non-central element. Unlike the definite case, no auxiliary place is exempted: congruence conditions modulo $M$ are imposed at all finite places other than $w$. It feeds the construction of norm-one elements with prescribed local behaviour used in [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsMaximalOrder.exists_isUnitOf_nrd_eq_one_sub_mem_of_nrd_eq`](thm.html#QuaternionAlgebra.IsMaximalOrder.exists_isUnitOf_nrd_eq_one_sub_mem_of_nrd_eq) and in the idelic factorisation statement [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsOrder.exists_nrd_eq_one_and_eq_finiteIdeleDiagonal_mul_mul_of_forall_nrd_eq_one_of_forall_isUnit`](thm.html#QuaternionAlgebra.IsOrder.exists_nrd_eq_one_and_eq_finiteIdeleDiagonal_mul_mul_of_forall_nrd_eq_one_of_forall_isUnit).
